Hi all,

This is to announce that sysstat 8.1.6 has been released and is 
available for download.

This version includes improvements and bug fixes mainly for pidstat and 
mpstat commands.

Sysstat 8.1.6 is available for download from my web page at:
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

247kB sysstat-8.1.6.tar.gz
204kB sysstat-8.1.6.tar.bz2
251kB sysstat-8.1.6-1.src.rpm
211kB sysstat-8.1.6-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat, pidstat and sa 
tools. Check out http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/features.html
to get a view of sysstat's main features.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> orange <dot> fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 8.1.5 are:
* [David Alan Gilbert]: Option -h added to pidstat. This option is used 
to display all activities horizontally on a single line.
* Fixed a bug in pidstat: When pidstat was used to monitor a process and 
all its threads (with pidstat's option -t), it could display weird 
values if the thread group leader terminated.
* Header line displayed by sar, iostat, mpstat, pidstat and sadf -H now 
includes the number of CPU.
* Use the correct word TGID instead of PID with pidstat -t.
* mpstat now displays stats for all interrupts, including NMI, LOC, etc.
* iostat's option -t now always displays the date and the time.
* Added option "--disable-documentation" to ./configure. Using this 
option prevents documentation files (including manual pages) from being 
installed.
* iconfig script updated. Now ask the user for documentation and isag 
script installation.
* NLS updated. Indonesian and Chinese (traditional) translations added.
* Makefile updated: There is now a dedicated target to install or 
uninstall NLS files.

